// Defect: two slices cannot be compared, though the compiler declares the
// methods that would compare them.
//
// newArrayRefTypeMethods in corelib/corenumber.c adds '==' and '!=' to the
// array-reference method table alongside 'len' and 'maxlen'. Their signature
// takes two array references whose region, permission and element type are all
// the placeholder 'unknownType', and no real slice type matches that, so
// overload selection finds no candidate and reports ErrorNoCandidate. A plain
// borrowed reference compares fine, so this is specific to slices rather than
// to reference comparison.
//
// What the comparison should mean is a separate question the reference manual
// does not settle -- identity of the data pointer and length, or equality of
// the elements. Either way the declaration promises an operation that cannot
// be reached from source.
//
// xfail: this file should compile clean.

fn sameSlice(a &[]i32, b &[]i32) Bool {
  a == b
}

fn differentSlice(a &[]i32, b &[]i32) Bool {
  a != b
}
